SCHEMA VERIFICATION vs. ich_gen/datasets/physionet_ich.py's docstring
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. hemorrhage_diagnosis_raw_ct.csv columns:
   EXPECTED (docstring / require_columns call):
     PatientNumber, SliceNumber, Intraventricular, Intraparenchymal,
     Subarachnoid, Epidural, Subdural, No_Hemorrhage, Fracture_Yes_No
   ACTUAL (real file, verified via pandas.read_csv):
     PatientNumber, SliceNumber, Intraventricular, Intraparenchymal,
     Subarachnoid, Epidural, Subdural, No_Hemorrhage, Fracture_Yes_No
   RESULT: EXACT MATCH, including casing. No COLUMN_MAP change needed.
   (Note: the raw file has a UTF-8 BOM before "PatientNumber" on disk;
   pandas.read_csv strips it automatically, so this does NOT cause a
   require_columns() failure -- confirmed empirically, not just assumed.)

2. ct_scans/ filename pattern:
   EXPECTED (docstring): "<PatientNumber>.nii[.gz]", and the loader
     builds this via `str(int(row["PatientNumber"]))`, e.g. "49.nii".
   ACTUAL (real files): zero-padded to 3 digits, e.g. "049.nii".
   RESULT: MISMATCH -- CONFIRMED BLOCKING BUG. build_samples(), as
   currently written, raises FileNotFoundError on the very first CSV
   row when run against the real data:
     "no volume found for patient 49 in .../ct_scans (tried
     ['.../ct_scans/49.nii', '.../ct_scans/49.nii.gz'])"
   The CSV/column parsing itself is NOT the problem (require_columns()
   passes cleanly) -- only the filename join is wrong. NOT patched in
   physionet_ich.py per task scope (only COLUMN_MAP fixes were
   pre-authorized); see scripts/smoke_test_physionet_ich.py and
   physionet_ich_smoke_test.log for the diagnostic proof that
   zero-padding to 3 digits (f"{int(row['PatientNumber']):03d}") makes
   every one of the 2814 CSV rows resolve to a real file.

3. masks/ filename pattern:
   EXPECTED (docstring): "<PatientNumber>_HGE_Seg.nii[.gz]"
   ACTUAL (real files): zero-padded 3-digit only, e.g. "049.nii" (no
     "_HGE_Seg" suffix).
   RESULT: MISMATCH in the docstring's description. NOT currently a
   functional bug because build_samples() never reads masks/ (it
   always sets lesion_size_mm3=None) -- but the docstring comment is
   wrong and should be corrected if/when mask-based lesion sizing is
   implemented for this site.
   Mask value check: masks are encoded as 0 / ~255 (not literal 0/1),
   i.e. an 8-bit-scaled binary mask, not strictly {0,1}.
   Mask coverage: all 75 patients that have a CT volume also have a
   mask file (75/75) -- contradicts the docstring's hedge "if present"
   implying some patients might lack a mask; in this v1.3.1 release,
   every released CT patient has a corresponding mask.

4. patient_demographics.csv:
   EXPECTED (docstring, lowercase): "patient_demographics.csv"
   ACTUAL (real file): "Patient_demographics.csv" (capital P).
   Also, the real file's header row differs from the docstring's
   informal description ("PatientNumber, age, gender, + patient-level
   labels"): actual first column is "Patient Number" (with a space,
   not "PatientNumber"), and the file has a two-row merged header
   (subtype columns Intraventricular/Intraparenchymal/... appear on a
   SECOND header line under a merged "Hemorrhage type..." cell, not a
   single flat header row). NOT currently a functional bug -- this
   file is not consumed by build_samples() at all (docstring already
   says so) -- but flagging both the filename casing (would matter on
   Linux, case-sensitive FS -- confirmed relevant since hp100 is
   Linux) and the two-row-header structure for whoever implements the
   demographic-subgroup analysis mentioned in the docstring.

5. Patient ID numbering / count:
   EXPECTED (docstring): "75 of the original 82 patients... #59-65
     confirmed missing"
   ACTUAL: CONFIRMED EXACTLY. Patient numbers run 049-130 inclusive
     (82 slots), with 059-065 (7 patients) missing, leaving 75.
     Verified both via directory listing and via
     df['PatientNumber'].unique() in the CSV.

6. HU units / skull HU sanity check (docstring's "verify skull HU
   ~700-3000" comment):
   Spot-checked patient 049 slice 0: HU range [-1022, 2830]. Confirmed
   the volumes are already in Hounsfield units with skull-range values
   present (~2830 max), consistent with the docstring's assumption --
   no separate DICOM rescale-slope/intercept step is needed for this
   site.

7. Per-patient slice count sanity check: patient 049 has 39 rows in
   the CSV (SliceNumber 1-39) and the corresponding NIfTI volume shape
   is (512, 512, 39) -- CSV slice count matches volume depth exactly,
   confirming the "CSV is 1-indexed, matches volume depth" assumption
   in the loader's inline comment.

SMOKE TEST RESULT (see scripts/smoke_test_physionet_ich.py and
physionet_ich_smoke_test.log for full output)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Unmodified build_samples(root) against real hp100 data: FAILS with
  FileNotFoundError on the filename-join bug described in item 2
  above. require_columns() itself does NOT fail (columns match).
- Diagnostic-only local re-implementation (same CSV/label logic, one
  deviation: zero-padded filename matching) against the same real
  data: all 2814 CSV rows resolve to a real CT file, 75/75 unique
  patients, label matrix shape (2814, 6) matching LABEL_COLUMNS order,
  all 75 patients have a mask file, and 2 spot-checked HU loads
  produced sane shapes/ranges.
- CONCLUSION: this is a real, small, well-understood, single-line bug
  (missing zero-padding in the ct_scans/<PatientNumber>.nii filename
  join inside build_samples()), NOT a deeper schema problem. No
  training/eval was run -- out of scope for this task.

